IMPORT prelude

-- Reciprocal Enforcement of Commonwealth Judgments (Repeal) Act 2019 (Singapore) -- commencement (s 1), the repeal of the
-- Reciprocal Enforcement of Commonwealth Judgments Act and which judgments it still reaches (s 2), the repeal of Part II of
-- the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act and the saving of its s 10 for existing orders (s 3), the deletion of
-- s 33(2) of the International Arbitration Act and its saving for older awards (s 4), and the Minister's two-year power to
-- make further saving regulations (s 5). That is the whole Act.
--
-- Edition: Act No. 24 of 2019, informal consolidation (the deposit's page furniture reads "version in force from 1/3/2023"),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RECJRA2019.txt. The only amendment annotated is "[Act 40 of 2019 wef
-- 01/03/2023]", against s 2(2)(d) (which speaks of "the General Division of the High Court"). The deposit does not state
-- the appointed date: s 1 leaves it to a Gazette notification, which was not retrieved. The arrangement at the top of the
-- deposit is out of step with the body (it numbers the short title 2); the body's numbers are used.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0259 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario
-- has asked a sharper question yet. For a judgment creditor or an award holder the answer is one question: does the old
-- law still reach my judgment or award after the repeal? The Act has five sections and all of them are here.
--
-- Not encoded: what the saved provisions themselves say (ss 2A, 3(1), (2), (3), (5) and 4 of the repealed Act, s 10 of the
-- Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act as it stood before the appointed date, s 33(2) of the International
-- Arbitration Act as it stood before that date). None of those texts was deposited with this Act, so the encoding says only
-- WHETHER a provision continues to apply, never what it then requires. The appointed date itself, the s 5 notifications
-- under the repealed Act, the REFJA s 3 orders, and any regulations under s 5 were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Reciprocal Enforcement of Commonwealth Judgments (Repeal) Act 2019 -- savings`

§§ `1 -- commencement`

-- s 1: the Act "comes into operation on a date that the Minister appoints by notification in the Gazette". s 2(2)(a) calls
-- that date "the appointed date".
GIVEN `the Minister has appointed a date by Gazette notification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointed date has arrived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act is in operation` IF
        `the Minister has appointed a date by Gazette notification`
    AND `the appointed date has arrived`

§§ `2 -- the repealed Act, and the judgments it still reaches`

-- s 2(1): "The Reciprocal Enforcement of Commonwealth Judgments Act (called in this Act the repealed Act) is repealed."
-- s 2(2)(a): "Despite subsection (1)", ss 2A and 3(1) and (2) of the repealed Act "continue to apply to a judgment obtained
-- before that date -- (i) in a superior court of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland; or (ii) in such
-- court of such part of the Commonwealth as is specified in a notification under section 5 of the repealed Act that was in
-- force immediately before that date".
DECLARE Court IS ONE OF
    `a superior court of the United Kingdom`
    `a court of the United Kingdom that is not a superior court`
    `a court of another part of the Commonwealth`
    `the General Division of the High Court of Singapore`
    `a court of a country outside the Commonwealth`

DECLARE Judgment HAS
    `court` IS A Court
    `was obtained before the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is specified in a s 5 notification in force immediately before the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was registered under s 3(1) and (2) of the repealed Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the registration was made before the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is registrable under the repealed Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (ii) turns on the notification being in force "immediately before that date": a court once specified, whose
-- notification had lapsed or been revoked by then, is outside (ii). The flag for (ii) is read only for a court of another
-- part of the Commonwealth.
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the judgment is of a court within s 2(2)(a)` IF
    CONSIDER `the judgment`'s `court`
    WHEN `a superior court of the United Kingdom` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court of another part of the Commonwealth`
        THEN `the judgment`'s `the court is specified in a s 5 notification in force immediately before the appointed date`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The saving keys on the date the judgment was OBTAINED, not the date it is registered: an old judgment may still be
-- brought under ss 3(1) and (2) after the repeal (subject to whatever those provisions require -- not deposited here).
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 2A and 3(1) and (2) of the repealed Act continue to apply` IF
        `the judgment`'s `was obtained before the appointed date`
    AND `the judgment is of a court within s 2(2)(a)` `the judgment`

-- s 2(2)(b): ss 2A and 3(3) of the repealed Act "continue to apply to a judgment registered under section 3(1) and (2) of
-- the repealed Act, including those provisions as applied by paragraph (a)".
--
-- A registration made before the appointed date is caught whatever its court; one made after it is caught only if it was
-- made through paragraph (a). That a registration after the appointed date has no other footing is an inference: after
-- the repeal, (a) is the only thing keeping ss 3(1) and (2) alive.
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 2A and 3(3) of the repealed Act continue to apply` IF
        `the judgment`'s `was registered under s 3(1) and (2) of the repealed Act`
    AND (    `the judgment`'s `the registration was made before the appointed date`
         OR  `ss 2A and 3(1) and (2) of the repealed Act continue to apply` `the judgment`)

-- s 2(2)(c): ss 2A and 3(5) of the repealed Act "continue to apply to a judgment mentioned in paragraph (a) registrable
-- under the repealed Act, including by the application of that paragraph".
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 2A and 3(5) of the repealed Act continue to apply` IF
        `ss 2A and 3(1) and (2) of the repealed Act continue to apply` `the judgment`
    AND `the judgment`'s `is registrable under the repealed Act`

-- s 2(2)(d): "section 4 of the repealed Act as in force immediately before the appointed date continues to apply to a
-- judgment obtained in the General Division of the High Court before that date." [Act 40 of 2019 wef 01/03/2023]
-- What s 4 provides is not in the deposit.
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 of the repealed Act continues to apply` IF
        `the judgment`'s `was obtained before the appointed date`
    AND `the judgment`'s `court` EQUALS `the General Division of the High Court of Singapore`

-- Taken together: does any saved provision of the repealed Act still reach the judgment? A judgment obtained on or after
-- the appointed date is never reached. (A summary of (a)-(d), not a phrase of the Act.)
GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the repealed Act still reaches the judgment` IF
        `ss 2A and 3(1) and (2) of the repealed Act continue to apply` `the judgment`
    OR  `ss 2A and 3(3) of the repealed Act continue to apply` `the judgment`
    OR  `ss 2A and 3(5) of the repealed Act continue to apply` `the judgment`
    OR  `s 4 of the repealed Act continues to apply` `the judgment`

§§ `3 -- Part II of the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act`

-- s 3(1): "Part II of the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act (Cap. 265, 2001 Ed.) (called in this section the
-- REFJA) is repealed."
-- s 3(2): "Despite subsection (1), section 10 of the REFJA as in force immediately before the appointed date continues to
-- apply in relation to an order made under section 3 of the REFJA before that date extending Part I of the REFJA to a part
-- of the Commonwealth to which the repealed Act applied, and that was in force immediately before that date."
-- What s 10 of the REFJA then provided is not in the deposit.
DECLARE Order HAS
    `was made under s 3 of the REFJA before the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `extends Part I of the REFJA to a part of the Commonwealth to which the repealed Act applied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was in force immediately before the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10 of the REFJA continues to apply in relation to the order` IF
        `the order`'s `was made under s 3 of the REFJA before the appointed date`
    AND `the order`'s `extends Part I of the REFJA to a part of the Commonwealth to which the repealed Act applied`
    AND `the order`'s `was in force immediately before the appointed date`

§§ `4 -- s 33(2) of the International Arbitration Act`

-- s 4(1): "Section 33 of the International Arbitration Act (Cap. 143A, 2002 Ed.) is amended by deleting subsection (2)."
-- s 4(2): "Despite subsection (1), section 33(2) of the International Arbitration Act as in force immediately before the
-- appointed date continues to apply to a foreign award (within the meaning of that Act) made before that date and
-- registrable under the repealed Act, including by the application of section 2(2)."
-- Here the saving keys on the date the award was MADE. What s 33(2) said is not in the deposit.
DECLARE Award HAS
    `is a foreign award within the meaning of the International Arbitration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was made before the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is registrable under the repealed Act, including by the application of s 2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the award` IS AN Award
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33(2) of the International Arbitration Act continues to apply to the award` IF
        `the award`'s `is a foreign award within the meaning of the International Arbitration Act`
    AND `the award`'s `was made before the appointed date`
    AND `the award`'s `is registrable under the repealed Act, including by the application of s 2(2)`

§§ `5 -- further saving and transitional regulations`

-- s 5: "For a period of 2 years after the appointed date, the Minister may, by regulations, prescribe such additional
-- provisions of a saving or transitional nature consequent on the enactment of any provision of this Act as the Minister
-- may consider necessary or expedient."
--
-- Time is counted here in whole months since the appointed date: fewer than 24 is inside the period. How the last day of
-- the two years is counted is not settled by the text (Interpretation Act rules were not read); treating 24 whole months
-- as outside is an inference.
GIVEN `whole months since the appointed date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the two-year period is running` IF
        `whole months since the appointed date` AT LEAST 0
    AND `whole months since the appointed date` LESS THAN 24

GIVEN `whole months since the appointed date` IS A NUMBER
      `the provision is of a saving or transitional nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is consequent on the enactment of a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considers it necessary or expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may prescribe the provision by regulations` IF
        `the two-year period is running` `whole months since the appointed date`
    AND `the provision is of a saving or transitional nature`
    AND `it is consequent on the enactment of a provision of this Act`
    AND `the Minister considers it necessary or expedient`
